Template: udm-iptv/profile
Type: select
Choices: BT (GB), Init7 (CH), KPN / XS4ALL / Freedom (NL), MagentaTV (DE), MEO (PT), PostTV (LU), Solcon (NL), Swisscom (CH), Telenor (NO), Tweak (NL), Vivo GVT (BR), Vivo SP (BR), Custom
Choices-C: bt, init7, kpn, magentatv, meo, posttv, solcon, swisscom, telenor, tweak, vivogvt, vivo, custom
Default: kpn
Description: IPTV provider profile:
 Select the provider defaults to apply. Hardware-specific WAN and LAN interfaces
 are detected on the console. Choose Custom to leave IPTV unconfigured and set
 every value yourself by running "udm-iptv install" after this package finishes.

Template: udm-iptv/telemetry
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Send identifying diagnostics to help improve udm-iptv?
 Reports go to the maintainer's Sentry project in the EU. They include
 configuration and changes, logs, failures, network state, a persistent
 installation ID, and your public IP and reverse-DNS hostname. This is not
 anonymous. Credentials and packet payloads must not be included.
 .
 IPTV works without reporting. Choose No to keep reporting disabled.
 You can change this later with "udm-iptv configure set --telemetry=false"
 or enable it with "--telemetry=true". See docs/telemetry.md for details.
